verses.tf_en:
① **«یٰۤاَیُّهَا النَّبِیُّ اِذَا طَلَّقْتُمُ النِّسَاۤءَ فَطَلِّقُوْهُنَّ لِعِدَّتِهِنَّ»** (O dear Prophet (Mohammed – peace and blessings be upon him)! When you people divorce women, divorce them at the time of their completing the appointed period,) — Addressing the Holy Prophet ﷺ as the supreme teacher and lawgiver of the community: O Prophet! When you (believers) find it necessary to divorce women, divorce them strictly in accordance with their prescribed waiting period (*'Iddah*)—which means pronouncing a single revocable divorce during a period of purity (*Tuhr*) in which no marital intimacy has taken place. Pronouncing three divorces at once, or divorcing during menstruation (*Haid*), is sinful, reprehensible (*Bid'i*), and severely prohibited in Islamic law;
② **«وَاَحْصُوا الْعِدَّةَ وَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ رَبَّكُمْ»** (And keep count of the appointed period; and fear Allah, your Lord;) — And accurately calculate and keep precise record of the duration of the waiting period; and fear Allah, your Cherishing Lord, by fulfilling all marital obligations with justice;
③ **«لَا تُخْرِجُوْهُنَّ مِنْ بُیُوْتِهِنَّ وَلَا یَخْرُجْنَ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ یَّاْتِیْنَ بِفَاحِشَةٍ مُّبَیِّنَةٍ»** (Do not expel them from their houses during the appointed period nor should they leave on their own, unless they bring about some matter of blatant lewdness;) — Do not force them out of their matrimonial homes during the waiting period, nor should they depart of their own accord out of anger; for lodging (*Sukna*) and financial support (*Nafaqah*) remain the binding legal duty of the husband throughout the 'Iddah; unless they commit flagrant indecency or blatant lewdness (*Fahishah Mubayyinah*);
④ **«وَتِلْكَ حُدُوْدُ اللّٰهِ وَمَنْ یَّتَعَدَّ حُدُوْدَ اللّٰهِ فَقَدْ ظَلَمَ نَفْسَهٗ»** (And these are the limits of Allah; and whoever crosses Allah’s limits has indeed wronged himself;) — These ordinances are the inviolable legal limits established by Allah; and whoever transgresses the boundaries of Allah has indeed grievously wronged his own soul and exposed himself to divine wrath;
⑤ **«لَا تَدْرِیْ لَعَلَّ اللّٰهَ یُحْدِثُ بَعْدَ ذٰلِكَ اَمْرًا»** (Do you not know, it is likely that Allah may send some new decree after this?) — The divine wisdom behind keeping the divorced wife in the home during 'Iddah is that you know not: perhaps Allah will soften hardened hearts during this period, rekindle mutual love, and bring about reconciliation (*Rujoo'*), healing the marriage before it becomes irreversible!

① **«فَاِذَا بَلَغْنَ اَجَلَهُنَّ فَاَمْسِكُوْهُنَّ بِمَعْرُوْفٍ اَوْ فَارِقُوْهُنَّ بِمَعْرُوْفٍ»** (So when they are about to reach their appointed term, hold them back with kindness or separate them with kindness,) — When the divorced women approach the end of their prescribed waiting period, the husband must make a definitive, honorable choice: either retain them in marriage with kindness, mutual respect, and genuine rectitude, or release them in an honorable, benevolent manner (*Fariqoohunna bi-Ma'roof*)—paying their remaining dowers and gifts without rancor, harm, or vindictiveness;
② **«وَّاَشْهِدُوْا ذَوَیْ عَدْلٍ مِّنْكُمْ وَاَقِیْمُوا الشَّهَادَةَ لِلّٰهِ»** (And make two just men among you as witnesses, and establish the testimony for Allah;) — And call to witness two upright, just Muslim men from among yourselves upon either reconciliation or final separation, to prevent future disputes; and O witnesses, uphold and deliver your testimony purely for the sake of Allah without bias or concealment;
③ **«ذٰلِكُمْ یُوْعَظُ بِهٖ مَنْ كَانَ یُؤْمِنُ بِاللّٰهِ وَالْیَوْمِ الْاٰخِرِ»** (With this is advised whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day;) — By these profound, equitable moral guidelines is admonished everyone who truly believes in Allah and the Day of Final Judgment;
④ **«وَمَنْ یَّتَّقِ اللّٰهَ یَجْعَلْ لَّهٗ مَخْرَجًا»** (And whoever fears Allah – Allah will create for him a way of deliverance.) — [A supreme, timeless Quranic guarantee]: And whoever fears Allah, observing His limits with mindful Taqwa in times of trial, Allah will create for him a triumphant way out of every worldly affliction, distress, and hardship!

① **«وَّیَرْزُقْهُ مِنْ حَیْثُ لَا یَحْتَسِبُ»** (And will provide him sustenance from a place he had never expected;) — And He will bestow lawful sustenance, unexpected relief, and divine blessings upon him from avenues and sources he could never have conceived or calculated in his wildest imagination;
② **«وَمَنْ یَّتَوَكَّلْ عَلَی اللّٰهِ فَهُوَ حَسْبُهٗ»** (And whoever relies on Allah – then Allah is Sufficient for him;) — And whoever places his total trust, reliance, and affairs into the hands of Allah (*Tawakkul*), then Allah alone is all-sufficient for him against every adversary and want;
③ **«اِنَّ اللّٰهَ بَالِغُ اَمْرِهٖ قَدْ جَعَلَ اللّٰهُ لِكُلِّ شَیْءٍ قَدْرًا»** (Indeed Allah will accomplish His command; indeed Allah has set a proper measure for all things.) — Verily, Allah accomplishes His sovereign decree and nothing in the heavens or earth can frustrate His will; indeed, Allah has pre-ordained a precise measure, fixed timing, and appointed term for every single circumstance and trial.

① **«وَالِّٰۤیْٔ یَئِسْنَ مِنَ الْمَحِیْضِ مِنْ نِّسَاۤئِكُمْ اِنِ ارْتَبْتُمْ فَعِدَّتُهُنَّ ثَلٰثَةُ اَشْهُرٍ»** (And for those of your women who have no hope of menstruation, if you doubt, the appointed period is three months –) — As for those of your women who have reached menopause and no longer expect menstruation due to advanced age, if you are in doubt regarding their legal status, their prescribed waiting period (*'Iddah*) upon divorce is three lunar months;
② **«وَّالِّٰۤیْٔ لَمْ یَحِضْنَ»** (And also for those who have not yet had menstruation;) — And likewise, the waiting period for young women who have not yet experienced their menstrual cycle is three lunar months;
③ **«وَاُولَاتُ الْاَحْمَالِ اَجَلُهُنَّ اَنْ یَّضَعْنَ حَمْلَهُنَّ»** (And the appointed period for the pregnant women is up to the time they deliver their burden;) — And as for pregnant women, their legally appointed term of 'Iddah terminates unconditionally the moment they deliver their child, whether the delivery takes place an hour after the divorce or after several months;
④ **«وَمَنْ یَّتَّقِ اللّٰهَ یَجْعَلْ لَّهٗ مِنْ اَمْرِهٖ یُسْرًا»** (And whoever fears Allah – Allah will create ease for him in his affairs.) — And whoever observes reverent Taqwa of Allah, adhering faithfully to His legal boundaries, Allah will facilitate ease, tranquility, and divine assistance in all his worldly and spiritual affairs!

① **«اَسْكِنُوْهُنَّ مِنْ حَیْثُ سَكَنْتُمْ مِّنْ وُّجْدِكُمْ وَلَا تُضَاۤرُّوْهُنَّ لِتُضَیِّقُوْا عَلَیْهِنَّ»** (Accommodate them where you also reside, according to your means, and do not harass them to make it difficult upon them;) — Provide the divorced women during their 'Iddah with decent, honorable lodging within your own means and capacity, wherever you reside; and never inflict psychological harassment, distress, or hostility upon them in order to force them into abandoning their home or forfeiting their financial rights;
② **«وَاِنْ كُنَّ اُولَاتِ حَمْلٍ فَاَنْفِقُوْا عَلَیْهِنَّ حَتّٰی یَضَعْنَ حَمْلَهُنَّ»** (And if they are pregnant, give them the provision till they deliver their burden;) — And if they are pregnant, you are legally bound to provide full financial maintenance, food, clothing, and medical care for them until they safely deliver their child;
③ **«فَاِنْ اَرْضَعْنَ لَكُمْ فَاٰتُوْهُنَّ اُجُوْرَهُنَّ وَاْتَمِرُوْا بَیْنَكُمْ بِمَعْرُوْفٍ»** (Then if they suckle the child for you, pay them its due; and consult with each other in a reasonable manner;) — Then, if they breastfeed the infant for you after delivery, compensate them with a fair and equitable nursing wage (*Ujoorahunna*); and settle the child's welfare through mutual, compassionate consultation (*Ma'roof*) with wisdom and goodwill;
④ **«وَاِنْ تَعَاسَرْتُمْ فَسَتُرْضِعُ لَهٗۤ اُخْرٰی»** (And if you create hardship for one another, the child will get another breast feeding nurse.) — But if you create mutual discord and reach an impasse regarding wages or nursing, then the father shall arrange another wet-nurse to suckle the infant, avoiding harm to both mother and child.

① **«لِیُنْفِقْ ذُوْ سَعَةٍ مِّنْ سَعَتِهٖ»** (Whoever has the capacity must give provisions according to his means;) — The man of abundant wealth and means must provide generous maintenance (*Nafaqah*) in accordance with his financial prosperity;
② **«وَمَنْ قُدِرَ عَلَیْهِ رِزْقُهٗ فَلْیُنْفِقْ مِمَّاۤ اٰتٰىهُ اللّٰهُ»** (And the one whose sustenance is restricted upon him, must give provisions from what Allah has given him;) — While he whose livelihood and resources are restricted must spend in proportion to what Allah has granted him; the law demands fairness without undue burden;
③ **«لَا یُكَلِّفُ اللّٰهُ نَفْسًا اِلَّا مَاۤ اٰتٰىهَا سَیَجْعَلُ اللّٰهُ بَعْدَ عُسْرٍ یُّسْرًا»** (Allah does not burden any soul except according to what He has given it; Allah will soon, after the hardship, create ease.) — Allah never burdens any soul beyond that which He has bestowed upon it; and let the impoverished take heart, for Allah will soon bring about profound ease, abundance, and relief following difficulty! [With this verse, Ruku 1 of Surah At-Talaq is concluded].

① **«اَللّٰهُ الَّذِیْ خَلَقَ سَبْعَ سَمٰوٰتٍ وَّمِنَ الْاَرْضِ مِثْلَهُنَّ»** (It is Allah Who has created the seven heavens, and seven earthly worlds like them;) — It is Allah alone Who created seven cosmic heavens in magnificent tiers, and of the earth a corresponding number of seven realms/strata in similar perfection;
② **«یَتَنَزَّلُ الْاَمْرُ بَیْنَهُنَّ لِتَعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّ اللّٰهَ عَلٰی كُلِّ شَیْءٍ قَدِیْرٌ»** (The command descends within them, so that you may know that Allah is Able to do all things,) — His sovereign divine command, cosmic decrees, and angelic revelations descend perpetually through all these cosmic spheres, in order that you may know and realize with unshakable certainty that Allah is Omnipotent over all things;
③ **«وَّاَنَّ اللّٰهَ قَدْ اَحَاطَ بِكُلِّ شَیْءٍ عِلْمًا»** (And that Allah’s knowledge encompasses everything.) — And that the infinite, all-encompassing knowledge of Allah encompasses every atom and entity in existence! [With this grand cosmic testimony, Surah At-Talaq is completed in its entirety].
